%%textfont Helvetica 16
%%begintext
  I wish I was a mole in the ground.
  I wish I was a mole in the ground.
  If I was a mole in the ground, I could tear that mountain down,
  Oh, I wish I was a mole in the ground.


  I wish I was a wave in the sea.
  I wish I was a wave in the sea.
  If I was a wave in the sea, you'd have no hold on me,
  Oh, I wish I was a wave in the sea.


  I wish I was the tide, deep and slow.
  I wish I was the tide, deep and slow.
  If I was the tide, deep and slow, I'd know just when to go,
  Oh, I wish I was the tide, deep and slow.

%%endtext

%%textfont Helvetica 12
%%begintext

Lyrics from Doc Watson and others:
%%endtext
%%textfont Helvetica 10
%%begintext
  
  If I was a mole in the ground, I'd tear that mountain down...


  If I was a lizard in the spring, I'd hear my darling sing...


  Little Tempey, let your hair roll down, and your bangs curl all around...


  Tempey wants a nine-dollar shawl...
  When I come o'er the hill, with that fifty-dollar bill,
  Gonna bring her that nine dollar shawl.


  If I was a little turtle dove, I’d fly away to my true love


  I don't like that railroad man...
  'Cause a railroad man, he'll kill you when he can
  And drink up your blood like wine.
   

  If I was a woolly boogie bee, I’d live in her cherry tree...
%%endtext

